-- title:
--   Prefix agreement survives concatenation and zero padding
-- statement:
--   Let $u,v,w$ be finite bit lists with $|v|=|w|$, and let $c\in\mathbb N$. Suppose that the first $c-|u|$ entries of $v$ form a prefix of $w$, where subtraction is truncated at zero. Write $\overline{uv}$ for the concatenation $uv$ padded by zero bits after its end, and similarly for $uw$. Then $$\overline{uv}(i)=\overline{uw}(i)\qquad\text{for every }i<c.$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ObservationRoundDrawSites.lean#L241-L263

